BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (lists to each agency's protocols and train crews in one 90-minute session. A hardware bundle) Tj T* (with a rugged tablet and portable printer is available at cost plus a small margin for agencies) Tj T* (without devices.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Unit economics are favorable on paper. Cloud and support costs are estimated at 45 dollars per) Tj T* (ambulance per year, giving about 87 percent gross margin on software. The main uncertainty is) Tj T* (customer acquisition. Volunteer agencies have small budgets and long decision cycles, and many) Tj T* (fund purchases through annual grants. Our plan is to sell through state and county volunteer) Tj T* (EMS associations, which hold regular trainings and can endorse a tool to many agencies at once,) Tj T* (and to help agencies write grant applications that cover the subscription. We have not yet) Tj T* (closed a paid contract, so the assumption that agencies will pay out of operating budgets or) Tj T* (grants remains unproven.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (Three categories compete for the same crews. Paper forms are free and familiar but produce) Tj T* (incomplete, illegible records and no dose timing. Full electronic patient care record systems) Tj T* (are comprehensive but typically priced for paid agencies, require connectivity or heavy setup) Tj T* (and take months to deploy. General-purpose note and form apps are cheap but lack medication) Tj T* (timers, hospital-ready reports and protocol-specific lists. Dosecheck Rural does less than a) Tj T* (full record system by design: it targets the moment of care and the moment of hand-off, works) Tj T* (offline from the first tap and costs a fraction of the alternatives. Our risk is that a large) Tj T* (incumbent could add an offline lite mode, though the incumbents we reviewed have shown little) Tj T* (interest in the smallest agencies.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Maren Okafor-Lindqvist, chief executive, is a senior in public health who volunteered for three) Tj T* (years with a rural ambulance service and led our interview program. Declan Varga, chief) Tj T* (technology officer, is a senior in computer science and built the offline sync engine. Priya) Tj T* (Thandani, clinical lead, is a nursing student and former emergency medical technician who) Tj T* (designed the hand-off report with input from two emergency department nurses. Tobias Reinholt,) Tj T* (product and design, is a junior in industrial design who led usability testing with crews. We) Tj T* (are advised informally by a retired county EMS director. We lack a team member with regulatory) Tj T* (and healthcare compliance experience, which we intend to address through an advisor.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (We completed 25 discovery interviews, defined the concept and built a working prototype. We) Tj T* (incorporated as an S corporation and launched a website. Two volunteer services are using the) Tj T* (prototype free of charge as pilot users, with 112 logged calls to date and a median of 6) Tj T* (seconds to record a medication. Pilot crews rated report usefulness at 4.4 out of 5, and both) Tj T* (directors have said they would pay but have not signed commitments.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our projected first-year plan is 40 ambulances across 16 agencies, producing about 12,000) Tj T* (dollars in subscription revenue against roughly 38,000 dollars in expenses, mainly part-time) Tj T* (contractor development, device costs and travel to association trainings. We project break-even) Tj T* (at roughly 200 ambulances, which we expect in year three. These figures rest on assumptions) Tj T* (about adoption speed that the pilots only partly support. To date we have spent about 4,200) Tj T* (dollars of personal savings.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Ask For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are seeking 25,000 dollars in competition funding. We would use 12,000 dollars to extend) Tj T* (development, including a pre-hospital protocol library and an accessibility review; 7,000) Tj T* (dollars to run six paid pilots with state association partners to test willingness to pay;) Tj T* (3,500 dollars for rugged devices and printers; and 2,500 dollars for legal review of data) Tj T* (handling and a healthcare compliance consultation. Beyond funding, we ask for introductions to) Tj T* (a regulatory advisor with health data experience and to program officers who fund rural) Tj T* (emergency services, since securing grant coverage is central to our sales strategy.) Tj ET
